"https://api.github.com/users/hermione521/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hermione521/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2015-12-24T01:24:09Z","updated_at":"2016-03-17T10:19:03Z","closed_at":"2016-03-17T10:19:03Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I am currently trying to download some javascript dependencies with a sandboxed gen-rule. I added the `requires-network` tag, but it appears that DNS resolution is broken. I confirmed that I could reach the localhost and that I could reach external hosts if I used the IP, but any attempts using host names fails.\n\nThis is reproducible with the following rule\n\n``` python\ngenrule(\n    name = \"network_test\",\n    srcs = glob([\"some/input/files/*\"]),\n    cmd = \"\"\"\n        # I started a server on the host on port 8000\n        curl localhost:8000\n\n        # google.com ip\n        curl 173.194.33.104\n\n        # This will fail\n        curl google.com\n    \"\"\",\n    outs = [\"out\"],\n    tags = [\"requires-network\"]\n)\n```\n\nThe first 2 curl commands succeed, and the third fails with `curl: (6) Could not resolve host: google.com`\n\nI'm on Ubuntu 15.10 with kernel 4.2.0-18.  This issue appeared both on bazel release 1.2 and master at the time of writing 9799246dc64429bc8f5b612c2596715180fe7592\n","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/following{/other_